# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# Playwright writes failure artefacts here (traces, screenshots, the HTML
# report). They are output, not source -- several MB of base64 and JPEGs per
# failed run -- so they stay out of the tree exactly as `.next/` does. A real
# run leaves them on disk for a human to open; nothing here is committed.
/test-results/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# The example is documentation and carries no secret: it names the two
# variables and explains why the token has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, which is a
# decision a developer should not have to reverse-engineer from the code. Every
# real .env* stays ignored above -- only this one name is re-included.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
